# data/spy.csv and data/rf.csv are frozen research artifacts (see CLAUDE.md
# hard rule 4: "Do not re-download or modify the frozen dataset"). With
# core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows checkouts), git normalises text
# files' line endings on checkout/commit, which can make an untouched file
# show as "modified" purely from CRLF/LF conversion. For a pre-registered
# dataset that must be reproducible byte-for-byte, that's not just noise —
# a real accidental edit could hide inside what looks like a routine
# line-ending diff. Marking these files "-text" tells git to leave them
# alone entirely: no line-ending conversion, ever, regardless of platform
# or autocrlf setting.
data/*.csv -text
